    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d562">

                <pb facs="0806" n="710" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg710"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Señor
                            Polo dé Bernabé.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: I am in receipt of your favor
                    of the 25th instant, informing me that you had telegraphed to Spanish consul at
                    New Orleans, ordering him to dispatch in ballast the vessel conducting to
                    Matanzas Mr. Albert Miller’s supplies, and had received reply that such
                    instructions would be complied with. In note of same date I informed you of name
                    of vessel and expected time of sailing.</p>
                <p>Accept my thanks for your prompt action in this matter, and believe me,</p>
                <p>Very truly, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William R. Day.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
